d3d11: Join the pipeline compile workers before the pipelines are freed.

PipelineCache declared its task_scheduler before the shader and pipeline maps, and members are
destroyed in the reverse order of their declaration, so a device released while pipelines were
still compiling freed those pipelines first and joined the workers compiling them after: a
worker could finish a compile on freed memory. (Commit ff4a98e fixed the scheduler's hang at
that join, not this.)

The scheduler is now declared last, so it is destroyed first: its destructor joins the workers,
which finish what they are compiling, while every map is still there.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 to 0008.
